experiment: objword
  SHORT RUN — 150000 ticks against a minimum of 1800000. derived: DOUBLE objname's 900k, and the reason is a measured one. §51's
  caregiver can only fire on a VOICED frame -- a silent larynx has no
  formants -- and delivery-fraction says this creature falls silent as it
  trains, so its realised dose is below §50's teacher by an unknown factor.
  vocallearn needed 3.4M at a 19x sparser reward clock and recorded density
  flipping its own sign. §51 asks how little the teacher has to KNOW: §50's
  was idealised twice over, since it saw the toy AND its target was this
  creature's own echo axis fitted in Phase A. M1c's caregiver re-pointed at
  the word it is SAYING removes both -- it compares two sounds, and
  object->word is never a term in the reward. Six arms, n unequal BY A
  POWER CALCULATION: §50's paired SD is 0.79, so a half-sized effect reads
  1.3 SE at n=12 and 2.2 SE at n=36. The primary contrast runs at 36; the
  4th-rung reference, the ceiling, the table-off arm and the yoked floor at
  12. kRead because every branch, including four VOIDs, prints a reading
  Everything below is printed for debugging and is NOT a
  measurement; this run cannot pass whatever it reads.

  the question      §51. §50's teacher is idealised TWICE: it knows which
                    object is present, and its target is this creature's own
                    echo axis fitted in Phase A. How little can it know?
  the teacher       M1c's caregiver re-pointed at THE WORD IT IS SAYING:
                    praise/scold on whether the produced formants came closer
                    than usual, per-word EMA baseline. It never looks at the
                    toy and its target is in the WORLD's units, not the
                    creature's. Object->word is never a term in the reward.
  the precedent     vocallearn ran this target and read FLAT on 3/3 (+0.7,
                    -1.4, +0.3) against a fixed target's +24.0 -- AT
                    context_slots = 0. Same missing index that made g3probe
                    null. §50 is why that is worth re-measuring.
  refused first     constant object-blind approval CANNOT work and needs no
                    run: the write is u = r * perturb_[i] with perturb_[i]
                    zero-mean and no Hebbian term on the held posture, so a
                    reward that does not evaluate the voice writes NOTHING in
                    expectation. T2 is that claim measured.
  session           150.0 s of simulated life x 120 sessions, 6 arms
  instrument        objword   trial seed 0000000001357639   120 sessions
                    another probe is another trial sequence: its numbers
                    are not comparable with these (~0.05 at 300 trials)

  CLAUSE 0 -- DOSE, NOT LIVENESS. T0 rewards a projection of the nine motor
  groups, which exist whether or not the creature is making a sound. T1 and T2
  can only fire on a VOICED frame, and delivery-fraction says this creature
  falls silent as it trains. An arm below 50% of T0's fire rate is
  UNDERPOWERED, not null. A T1 praise fraction outside [0.35, 0.65] means the
  EMA baseline is not being straddled and the arm is void.
    T0.RET     n 12/12  slots 2(ask 2)  present 1.0000  occ 0.8917  fired 1.0000 (1.00x T0)  praise 0.493  mean|r| 0.0781  probes 240
    T1.RET     n 36/36  slots 2(ask 2)  present 1.0000  occ 0.7139  fired 0.7747 (0.77x T0)  praise 0.500  mean|r| 0.5000  probes 720
    T1.RET.D   n 36/36  slots 2(ask 2)  present 1.0000  occ 0.6903  fired 0.7646 (0.76x T0)  praise 0.518  mean|r| 0.5000  probes 720
    T1.ORACLE  n 12/12  slots 2(ask 2)  present 1.0000  occ 0.5000  fired 0.8226 (0.82x T0)  praise 0.554  mean|r| 0.5000  probes 240
    T1.BASE    n 12/12  slots 0(ask 0)  present 0.0000  occ 0.0000  fired 0.8251 (0.83x T0)  praise 0.513  mean|r| 0.5000  probes 240
    T2.RET     n 12/12  slots 2(ask 2)  present 1.0000  occ 0.9167  fired 0.4244 (0.42x T0)  praise 0.498  mean|r| 0.5000  probes 240
    *** AN ARM IS BELOW HALF OF T0's FIRE RATE. Pre-registered as
    UNDERPOWERED rather than null -- a teacher that rarely fires has not
    been tested, and reporting it as a refusal would be the error
    liveness-is-not-dose exists to prevent.

  CLAUSE 1 -- §49 AND §50 BOTH MEASURED THE RETINAL INDEX WITH THE CAREGIVER
  SILENT. Source 5 reads kVision, so added auditory drive should not touch it,
  and that has never been measured. Bar is +0.20 excess against §50's +0.3165.
    T0.RET     ctx_match 0.5333  null 0.5549  excess -0.0216   <-- BELOW BAR
    T1.RET     ctx_match 0.5361  null 0.5821  excess -0.0460   <-- BELOW BAR
    T1.RET.D   ctx_match 0.5375  null 0.5830  excess -0.0455   <-- BELOW BAR
    T2.RET     ctx_match 0.5333  null 0.5461  excess -0.0128   <-- BELOW BAR

  CLAUSE 2 -- THE PROBE MUST BE SILENT. If the word is audible at probe,
  M1b's INNATE ear->larynx route produces the right sound with nothing
  learned, and every number above is an echo. Teaching-window heard fraction
  is derived: (900 - 500)/(1400 - 500) = 0.4444.
    T0.RET     probe heard 0.0000 (want 0.0000)  teach heard 0.0000 (want 0.0000)
    T1.RET     probe heard 0.0000 (want 0.0000)  teach heard 0.4444 (want 0.4444)
    T1.RET.D   probe heard 0.0000 (want 0.0000)  teach heard 0.4444 (want 0.4444)
    T1.ORACLE  probe heard 0.0000 (want 0.0000)  teach heard 0.4444 (want 0.4444)
    T1.BASE    probe heard 0.0000 (want 0.0000)  teach heard 0.4444 (want 0.4444)
    T2.RET     probe heard 0.0000 (want 0.0000)  teach heard 0.4444 (want 0.4444)

  CLAUSE 3 -- THE PRIMARY, axis_sep: the projection of (mean voice | object 1
  - mean voice | object 0) onto the Phase A echo axis over |axis|^2, so 1.0 is
  FULL compliance with the separation the two words ask for. Signed, zero
  expectation under drift, no fitted split. THE SAME RULER FOR EVERY ARM,
  including the ones whose reward uses a different target -- scoring each arm
  on its own reward's currency is how a verdict gets fitted to the data.
    T0.RET     axis_sep +0.0583 +- 0.0306  (n 12, 8/12 > 0)   §50 reproduced -- THE 4TH RUNG, without which a null below says nothing
    T1.RET     axis_sep -0.0288 +- 0.0242  (n 36, 18/36 > 0)   THE CLAIM: the caregiver never looks at the toy
    T1.RET.D   axis_sep -0.0297 +- 0.0284  (n 36, 16/36 > 0)   word DRAWN -- the CO-OCCURRENCE destroyed, everything else identical
    T1.ORACLE  axis_sep -0.2755 +- 0.1615  (n 12, 5/12 > 0)   index pinned to the true object -- T1's CEILING
    T1.BASE    axis_sep +0.0122 +- 0.0449  (n 12, 7/12 > 0)   bias table OFF -- catches the ASSOCIATION route (g2cond says it is shut)
    T2.RET     axis_sep +0.0311 +- 0.0414  (n 12, 7/12 > 0)   YOKED reward -- the arithmetic floor, and arrival vs content

  SECONDARY, IN T1's OWN CURRENCY AND EXCLUDED FROM THE VERDICT: formant
  error at the silent probe toward the OTHER word minus toward its OWN word,
  so positive means the voice sits closer to the word this object is named by.
    T0.RET     perr(other) - perr(own) +0.0127
    T1.RET     perr(other) - perr(own) +0.0029
    T1.RET.D   perr(other) - perr(own) -0.0021
    T1.ORACLE  perr(other) - perr(own) +0.1071
    T1.BASE    perr(other) - perr(own) -0.0035
    T2.RET     perr(other) - perr(own) -0.0026

  CLAUSE 4 -- THE 4TH RUNG. T0.RET must reproduce §50 at >= +0.30 (half of
  +0.5875) for a null on T1 to be interpretable. It reads +0.0583: FAIL

  CLAUSE 5 -- THE VERDICT. Paired by creature, bar 2 SE, sign unconstrained.
    T1.RET - T1.RET.D   +0.0009  (paired SE 0.0291, 0.0 SE)   <-- PRIMARY
    T1.RET - T2.RET     -0.0534  (paired SE 0.0683)
    T1.RET - T1.BASE    -0.0345  (paired SE 0.0532)
    in these units 1.0 is FULL compliance, so 2 SE = 0.0582 is the smallest
    share of the asked-for gesture this run can resolve.

    VOID (clause 0, 1 or 3): the retinal index did not survive a speaking caregiver. §51 says nothing about teaching.
